[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186439269","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5186439269","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5186439269,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNSLIZQ","user":{"login":"Leonardo-Ma","id":68714883,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NzE0ODgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68714883?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma","html_url":"https://github.com/Leonardo-Ma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leonardo-Ma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T01:21:43Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T01:21:43Z","body":"Could reasoning and possible approaches be expanded? The linked issue is very specific about **_scripts_** overriding engine defaults, but it's being suggested as a new approach instead of changing engine node default values to avoid breaking compatibility with previous versions. Something I don't see being explained in the issue, here, in the salvaged PR or in any of the PRs/issues that are being referenced to this (the linked chat message also doesn't open for me, so can't check that).\r\n\r\nIf it's also only applied when created by the editor, doesn't that mean two versions of every single instance to be maintained? That seems a nightmare?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186439269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5190318813","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5190318813","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5190318813,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNV363Q","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T09:57:12Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T09:57:12Z","body":">  it's being suggested as a new approach instead of changing engine node default values to avoid breaking compatibility with previous versions.\r\n\r\nWell, that's just one possible usage. #119020 does change properties, but they are not intended to be defaults; they are meant to make the node more usable _in the editor_ out of the box. The customized \"defaults\" should be irrelevant outside the editor.\r\n\r\nFor changes that work around compatibility, the code should be explicitly marked with `#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED`, so it's easy to identify as such. And we do have a similar mechanism already, for project settings when creating new projects.\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ac7ef92b78e66c6fd8e10144ac83a6ac997c7224/editor/editor_node.cpp#L8418-L8420\r\n\r\n> If it's also only applied when created by the editor, doesn't that mean two versions of every single instance to be maintained? That seems a nightmare?\r\n\r\nThere is a risk if it's overused I guess. I think the editor defaults should be mentioned in the docs.\r\n\r\nHowever this PR only introduces the notification, the details on its usage in the engine are yet to be decided in the subsequent PRs. There are just numerous cases where it can be useful.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5190318813/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194866831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5194866831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5194866831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNaNgjw","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T17:07:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T17:07:09Z","body":"This leads to adding blocks of editor only code in each Node that uses it.\r\n\r\nUsers can add nodes to a scene in the editor from code, and if they want to use editor defaults they may try to send the notification manually. The proposal mentions wanting the notification from code, and this would be a workaround for that. However, `instantiate_object_properties` doesn't get called so it may be inaccurate.\r\n\r\nI wanted to mention an alternative approach to consider, since I haven't really seen it brought up.\r\nWe could have a single method in editor code that takes the new Node as an argument and sets the default values, eg:\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid set_editor_defaults(Node *p_node) {\r\n\tLabel *label = Object::cast_to<Label>(p_node);\r\n\tif (label) {\r\n\t\tlabel->set_text(\"Label\");\r\n\t}\r\n\tDecal *decal = Object::cast_to<Decal>(p_node);\r\n\t//etc\r\n}\r\n```\r\nThere can be a signal emitted on EditorNode from `instantiate_object_properties` that connects to this method (in EditorNode or maybe a new file b/c of includes). Other places / modules can connect to it too to configure their nodes separately.\r\nWe can emit a signal on EditorInterface for users to connect to. And probably expose a method that calls `instantiate_object_properties` in case the user makes nodes in the editor and wants editor defaults.\r\n\r\nThis way editor-only code isn't added to each node. Users wouldn't have to make their Nodes tool scripts to have editor defaults, it can be in a separate tool script. \r\nThis would also allow users to override the defaults of any Node that gets created in the editor, which seems useful for plugins to configure defaults for a project.\r\nThere are some drawbacks though, like more merge conflicts in this method, and you need to find this to find the defaults for a node.\r\nPrivate variables also won't be accessible, but since the purpose is to set editor default values, it shouldn't need private variables.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nShould we have this for Resources too?\r\nIf a Resource is part of a Node the Node can set the default of the Resource, but that is different than changing the editor defaults of Resources themselves.\r\nIt may need to be a separate notification(/signal) anyway so we can wait until its needed.\r\n\r\n\r\nAlso cc @godotengine/xr since the proposal is mainly about XR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194866831/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5195224636","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5195224636","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5195224636,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNajWPA","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T17:41:26Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T17:41:26Z","body":"Admittedly we have a very chaotic setup for editor-only code which would be nice to re-evaluate.\r\n- It reminded me of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/89160 again.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5195224636/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5197160717","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5197160717","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5197160717,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNcZhDQ","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T20:47:54Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T20:47:54Z","body":"> We could have a single method in editor code that takes the new Node as an argument and sets the default values\r\n\r\nThat sounds like sensible approach.\r\n\r\nA signal could be even connected in plugins, so e.g. particle plugin could be responsible for setting particle defaults, so we don't have a single super method for handling everything.\r\n\r\nOne downside is that many callbacks might get connected to such signal, each checking whether the provided node is of expected type, which might eventually make instantiating nodes slower. Although it does not cause problems with `settings_changed()`, so it's probably fine.\r\n\r\nAnother thing is that the order of callbacks for signal can't be reasonably guaranteed, unlike for a notification. Multiple callbacks customizing one node can easily mess up each other's settings.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5197160717/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5240882431","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5240882431","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5240882431,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOGGE_w","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-10T13:23:15Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T13:23:15Z","body":"Changed notification to a signal and fixed some cases where object wasn't initialized.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5240882431/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5256310616","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5256310616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5256310616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOUzvWA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-11T17:04:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T17:04:31Z","body":"With this new approach, is it still possible to implement https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122066 in a way that doesn't break [encapsulation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/53295)?\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n#ifdef TOOLS_ENABLED\r\nvoid Decal::_notification(int p_what) {\r\n\tswitch (p_what) {\r\n\t\tcase NOTIFICATION_READY: {\r\n\t\t\tEditorInterface::get_singleton()->connect(\"object_created_in_editor\", Callable(this, \"_object_created_in_editor\"));\r\n\t\t} break;\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid Decal::_object_created_in_editor(Object *p_object) {\r\n\tprint_line(\"test\");\r\n\r\n\t// Set improved defaults for newly created Decal nodes in the editor.\r\n\t// This does not affect Decals created by code, or Decals created in older versions of Godot.\r\n\tDecal* d = Object::cast_to<Decal>(p_object);\r\n\tif (d) {\r\n\t\td->set_size(Vector3(2.0, 1.0, 2.0));\r\n\t\td->set_upper_fade(0.0);\r\n\t\td->set_lower_fade(0.0);\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor this to compile, I need to `#include \"editor/editor_interface.h\"`, but Decal is part of `scene/`. (Either way, it doesn't seem to get called anyway.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5256310616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5256388547","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5256388547","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5256388547,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOU4fww","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-11T17:11:37Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T17:12:31Z","body":"It's not possible in the class itself. You'd have to add DecalEditorPlugin, which handles the signal. It's more involved, but avoids adding editor-specific code to scene classes.\r\n\r\n> Either way, it doesn't seem to get called anyway.\r\n\r\nYou should use `callable_mp()`, Callable() is only for registered methods.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5256388547/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5270254448","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5270254448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5270254448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOiGzcA","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-12T17:36:05Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T17:36:05Z","body":"> It's not possible in the class itself. You'd have to add DecalEditorPlugin, which handles the signal. It's more involved, but avoids adding editor-specific code to scene classes.\r\n\r\nThanks for the advice, I updated https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122066 accordingly :slightly_smiling_face: ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5270254448/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5294553384","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5294553384","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5294553384,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO5R5KA","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T14:37:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T14:39:57Z","body":"Y'know, now that I think about it, both the signal and the notification don't have to be mutually exclusive features.\r\n\r\nBecause, yes, with a signal we do not break encapsulation and allow addons to inject their own code, but one could argue some users would rather not be bothered to make their own editor plugin for a few tweaks on object creation.\r\nThe logic could be present in the original script to keep code less spread out, and this may need to run in the editor with `@tool`, anyway, for other miscellaneous custom behavior.\r\n\r\nEither way we would have to choose one or the other within Godot's codebase.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5294553384/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297156868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5297156868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5297156868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO7wzBA","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T19:08:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T19:13:46Z","body":"You don't really need a plugin to use this signal in your scripts, you only have to avoid using EditorInterface directly.\r\n```GDScript\r\n@tool\r\nclass_name TestClass extends Node\r\n\r\nfunc _init() -> void:\r\n\tif Engine.has_singleton(&\"EditorInterface\"):\r\n\t\tEngine.get_singleton(&\"EditorInterface\").object_created_in_editor.connect(initialize_editor_stuff, CONNECT_ONE_SHOT)\r\n\r\nfunc initialize_editor_stuff(object: Object):\r\n\tif object == self:\r\n\t\tprint(\"Test\")\r\n```\r\nThis works and does not break scripts at runtime. It's a bit more involved than notification though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5297156868/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5385306589","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5385306589","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5385306589,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQP1B3Q","user":{"login":"romgerman","id":1517367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTczNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1517367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman","html_url":"https://github.com/romgerman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/romgerman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-23T09:30:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-23T09:30:24Z","body":"> Creating Scripts and Shaders don't emit the signal, but that seems fine\r\n\r\nWhy is that if they are still Resources? That special treatment for Scripts is exactly why some things is impossible to do in the editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5385306589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5385836393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122058#issuecomment-5385836393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122058","id":5385836393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQQVXaQ","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githu